Inbound contributions to this directory
---------------------------------------

Contributions to `cloister/vault/` are offered under BOTH the
Apache License 2.0 and the AGPL-3.0-or-later that governs cloister as
a whole. Cloister distributes them under the AGPL; the additional
Apache 2.0 grant exists so that improvements made here can flow back
to the notme original, or into a shared permissively-licensed package,
without a per-contribution relicensing negotiation.

WHY THIS IS RECORDED NOW RATHER THAN WHEN IT IS NEEDED. The lift
described above, and any return of work to notme, have so far been
legitimate for one reason: a single author holds copyright in every
line of this directory (verified 2026-08-04 — `git log` over `vault/`
shows one person under two committer names). A copyright holder may
license their own work however they choose, so nothing had to be
agreed in advance.

That stops at the FIRST contribution from anyone else. Their work
would be AGPL-only, cloister could not offer it back under Apache 2.0,
and the two copies would be permanently unable to converge — the
licence direction only runs one way, since AGPL can consume permissive
but permissive cannot consume AGPL. Stating the inbound terms while
sole authorship still holds is what keeps that door open; stating them
afterwards requires going back and asking.

